Note: Format
NAME Category_id Produst_id Level_id M# Level(s) P# Level(s) >|<|=  T# threshold(s)
 

NOTE: M/S*1.94 -> KNOT
      1 INCH = 25.4 
      1 MM = 25.4 KG/M2 
      1 M = 3.28 feet

NOTE: (1) FIRW (fire weather) belongs to discipline 2, categroy 4. But current Table 4.2-2-4 only 
          Haines index (parameter #2) is defined. For Frosburg index, #3 is defined by us here
      (2) AP1h, AP3h and AP6h are all share same category# (1) and same parameter# (8), only time
          ranges are different but not shown here. The time range will be considered in code
      (3) Fog is not defined in cloud category (Table 4.2-0-6), so use "cloud work function", 
          i.e. parameter # 193, to define it
      (4) FIRW: Hainse_index: (2,3,4),(5),(6), using following:
                 (>=2 and <5), (>=5 and <6),(>=6 and <7) 
      (5) SN1h, SN3h, SN6h thresholds are designed with an implicit SLR of 10:1 (1", 3", 6", 12" accumulation depths)
